@varun-sundar-rabindranath What do you mean by checking for the different errors directly? I'm not sure I understand.

The reason I'm using `engine_client.add_lora` is that the frontend doesn't know about the different ways that a lora adapter can be loaded (ie a download from hf hub, or loading from local files) and it doesn't know about the different ways an adapter can fail (malformed files, rank too high, weights not matching the layers loaded in the model etc.)

I don't think it's possible to check all of the error cases without actually trying to load the adapter, and the engine is responsible for knowing how to load it
